From aae91fafa183b407d7c0707a1b57a12380b07046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:22:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo: route RX_BIAS
 to MCLK

With only the EAR (earpiece) path powered, nothing keeps the WCD9340
master clock on: the output powers up with the codec clock off, SLIMbus
logs "overflow error on RX port 0" and the earpiece stays silent. It only
played while the speaker path happened to hold MCLK.

Add the "RX_BIAS", "MCLK" route, as in Microsoft's Android DT and on the
other WCD934x boards (db845c, beryllium). Verified on the Duo: the EAR
output plays on its own and the overflow is gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EJcJH42jMtxxhTuvKvyeRV
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi    | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
index 64722493e..94ea3eeec 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo-mic.dtsi
@@ -14,8 +14,13 @@
 	 * driver is a module) the amp is already runtime-suspended then (regmap cache-only): the Bandgap (0x3103) and
 	 * RDAC (0x311c) writes fail with -EBUSY, DAPM still marks them on and never writes them again -> silent speaker.
 	 * With the route the path powers with the stream, after ASoC has resumed the amp.
+	 *
+	 * RX_BIAS needs the codec MCLK, as in Microsoft's DT and on every other WCD934x board (db845c, beryllium):
+	 * without it the analog outputs (EAR earpiece, LINEOUT) power up with the codec clock off -> silent earpiece
+	 * and "overflow error on RX port 0" on SLIMbus.
 	 */
-	audio-routing = "DMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+	audio-routing = "RX_BIAS", "MCLK",
+			"DMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
 			"DMIC2", "MIC BIAS3",
 			"SpkrLeft IN", "SPK1 OUT";
 
